NEARS-1963 QA — OTP PinCodeTextField tap-to-focus defect
Device: emulator-5560, package com.izzes.nears.nears_nears_1963_otp_a11y

REPRO: verification screen reached via forget_pass_screen -> +971500000263 -> Request OTP.
Live-reported PIN field bounds center tapped: adb shell input tap 672 1717
(bounds [147,1603][1197,1831], confirmed via two-dump rule, hint="Verification Code")

SIGNAL 1 — Android IME service state (before/after tap):
  $ adb shell dumpsys input_method | grep mInputShown
  mInputShown=false        <- stays false after the tap (keyboard never opens)

SIGNAL 2 — accessibility tree after tap + `input text "123456"`:
  EditText enabled=true focused=false text=''   <- digits never landed
  Verify button enabled=false                    <- stays disabled (needs 6 digits)

SIGNAL 3 — Flutter's OWN FocusManager (authoritative, non-adb-projected),
  captured live via the Dart VM service (ext.flutter.debugDumpFocusTree),
  immediately after the same tap:
  FocusScopeNode#8cf68(_ModalScopeState<dynamic> Focus Scope [PRIMARY FOCUS])
    (current route's scope) with 3 leaf FocusNode children —
    NONE of the 3 ever shows [IN FOCUS PATH] / PRIMARY FOCUS after the tap.
  i.e. focus never leaves the route scope and lands on any leaf node
  (one of those 3 leaves is _pinFocusNode).

REPRODUCTION MATRIX (all show the identical failure):
  - TalkBack/touch-exploration ON  -> fails (mInputShown=false)
  - TalkBack/touch-exploration OFF -> fails (mInputShown=false) -- rules out an
    a11y-only regression; this breaks NORMAL tap-to-type too, not just TalkBack's
    tap-to-focus handoff (the ticket's OPEN RISK, confirmed AND found broader
    than flagged).
  - Fresh cold-restarted app process -> fails identically (rules out session/
    TalkBack-toggling state contamination from this QA session).

POSITIVE CONTROL (proves the tooling/instrument is alive, same session, same
build, identical methodology `adb shell input tap` + `adb shell input text`):
  Forgot-password screen's ordinary Phone EditText (untouched by this diff):
    tap -> mInputShown=true, focused=true, typed text lands correctly.
  See control-phone-field-focuses-normally.xml.

SCOPE: only file touched by this ticket's single commit is
UserApp/lib/features/verification/screens/verification_screen.dart (confirmed:
`git log --oneline main..HEAD -- <file>` = 1 commit). The diff's only
behavioral additions on this screen are: passing an app-owned FocusNode/
TextEditingController into PinCodeTextField (previously package-internal),
autoDisposeControllers:false, and the outer Semantics(excludeSemantics:true,
onTap:...) wrapper. One or more of these broke the package's internal
GestureDetector -> _onFocus() -> _focusNode.requestFocus() wiring (pin_code_fields
8.0.1, lib/src/pin_code_fields.dart lines ~844-852, ~954-966). Root-causing the
exact mechanism is an engineering task; this file documents the live, repeated,
control-validated PROOF that it is broken, not the fix.

